{"id": 31, "ts": 1781726500.0912526, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I concur with Sofia\u2019s assessment. Candidate\u202fC demonstrates concrete evidence across the core safety criteria: he keeps calm in a crisis (stress resilience), makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality), is 100\u202f% reliable with excellent attention (operational reliability and information accuracy), and creates a positive crew atmosphere (crew\u2011cooperation). While his communication style is difficult and he is less eager for further education, the positive crew\u2011atmosphere observation suggests these issues do not undermine his ability to work effectively in the cockpit. In contrast, Candidate\u202fD, despite strong concentration and problem\u2011solving, lacks any documented evidence of decision\u2011making quality or crew\u2011cooperation, and his hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all perception remain unmitigated concerns. Therefore, Candidate\u202fC offers the strongest overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
